intent: Fix B7's bisect interpretation for nool 7.0.0's attestation-knot indirection: the integrity-driver mints an unconditional per-landing syntax-attestation knot invisible to nool log but not excluded from debug bisect's search space, so 'First bad Knot' can name a wrapper knot with no resolvable intent. b7_regression_localization.py now unwraps 'Attest ... for <prefix>' to the real knot it attests and judges correctness against that; summarize.py's B7 table surfaces the resolved intent and via_attestation prefix. Corrected result: nool resolves to landing 6 (off-by-one before the true landing 7 culprit), not a total miss
